# Dipole selection rules of the crystal-orbital diagrams (crystod --diagram); testsuite section 4
# Every --diagram engine (extended Hueckel, --pyscf, --vasp) ends each k point with
# the block below: the VBM -> CBM transition is allowed for the Cartesian
# polarization components listed, or forbidden, by
# Gamma_f* x Gamma_V x Gamma_i containing the identity of the little group of k
# (vertical transitions; ISO-IR labels of the levels). When the band edge is
# forbidden, the allowed occupied -> empty pair of smallest energy follows.
# x, y, z are the Cartesian axes of the input POSCAR; when they are rotated against
# the crystal axes, an allowed direction that is not an axis is printed as a vector
# (e.g. "allowed (0 1 -1)", see doc/crystod.md section 4).
# In the HTML page, click one crystal orbital and then another: the verdict
# appears next to the second level; a click on empty space clears it.
# POSCAR_Cu2O: cuprite (Pn-3m), the structure of ../test_POSCARs/224_PPOSCAR_Ag2O
# with a = 4.2696 A (the extended-Hueckel tables have no Ag parameters).
# Output below: the dipole blocks and, for Cu2O, the crystal levels around the gap
# (lines in between omitted, marked ...).

$ crystod --diagram -c ../test_POSCARs/221_PPOSCAR_SrTiO3 --co-left SrTi --co-right O3
...

* Dipole selection rules at GM (0,0,0) *
   VBM GM5- #1 (-13.80 eV) -> CBM GM5+ #1 (-12.38 eV): allowed (x, y, z)
   (vertical transitions in the little group of k; polarizations in the Cartesian axes x, y, z of the input cell)

...
* Dipole selection rules at R (1/2,1/2,1/2) *
   VBM R5- #1 (-13.60 eV) -> CBM R5+ #5 (-11.51 eV): allowed (x, y, z)
   (vertical transitions in the little group of k; polarizations in the Cartesian axes x, y, z of the input cell)

...
* Dipole selection rules at X (0,1/2,0) *
   VBM X2+ #1 (-13.81 eV) -> CBM X2- #1 (-12.30 eV): forbidden
   first allowed: X5+ #4 (-13.83 eV) -> X2- #1 (-12.30 eV), dE = 1.53 eV: allowed (x, z)
   (vertical transitions in the little group of k; polarizations in the Cartesian axes x, y, z of the input cell)

...
* Dipole selection rules at M (1/2,1/2,0) *
   VBM M2+ #1 (-13.60 eV) -> CBM M5+ #2 (-10.26 eV): forbidden
   first allowed: M5- #6 (-14.12 eV) -> M5+ #2 (-10.26 eV), dE = 3.86 eV: allowed (z)
   (vertical transitions in the little group of k; polarizations in the Cartesian axes x, y, z of the input cell)

...
